{"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "048M", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$k$", "MATH_0002": "$B$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Spec(k)$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Spec(k) \\to B$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2148a456757d1fd1835d899d5055ec1b82fc840c5633223f54b32438d4f61516", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3c3b65600489d3fbbccf60d768a4b6229564989849b876cb8b1055624624088b", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn the following definition we use the terminology ``<MATH_0001> is a field\nover <MATH_0002>'' to mean that <MATH_0003> comes equipped with a morphism\n<MATH_0004>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:208adff03e79d84e746161535d820b4e874ec83c97b974fca06a32261c2c4e2f", "unit_id": "tag:048M:prose-0006"}
{"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "048M", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$B$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$j : R \\to U \\times_B U$", "MATH_0005": "$B$", "MATH_0006": "$\\phi : U \\to X$", "MATH_0007": "$R$", "MATH_0008": "$U(k) \\to X(k)$", "MATH_0009": "$s, t : R(k) \\to U(k)$", "MATH_0010": "$k$", "MATH_0011": "$B$", "MATH_0012": "$\\phi : U \\to X$", "MATH_0013": "$R$", "MATH_0014": "$R$", "MATH_0015": "$\\phi(\\overline{u}) = \\phi(\\overline{u}')$", "MATH_0016": "$X(k)$", "MATH_0017": "$\\overline{u}, \\overline{u}' \\in U(k)$", "MATH_0018": "$k$", "MATH_0019": "$B$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0003": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0003": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-set-theoretically-invariant}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f5028760b2e63b4dc88d01865ae708f92fef399c7ff3610a3490a52cf469e6ec", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c184a8f0aec743045a0ed9923646b3c6a439719aa6f7c92e48dfa698d49d7e6c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme, and let <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a pre-relation over <MATH_0005>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> We say <MATH_0006> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>set-theoretically <MATH_0007>-invariant<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nif and only if the map <MATH_0008> equalizes the two maps\n<MATH_0009> for every algebraically closed field <MATH_0010>\nover <MATH_0011>.\n<STRUCT_0003> We say <MATH_0012> <TEXTITOPEN_0002>separates orbits<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>, or\n<TEXTITOPEN_0003>separates <MATH_0013>-orbits<TEXTITCLOSE_0003> if it is set-theoretically <MATH_0014>-invariant and\n<MATH_0015> in <MATH_0016> implies that\n<MATH_0017> are in the same orbit\nfor every algebraically closed field <MATH_0018> over <MATH_0019>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8baa69b6e505a3fd1534b8148fae4dc22c98518ffe5f2fe6349cc25c2af8682b", "unit_id": "tag:048V:statement"}
{"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "048M", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{example-not-invariant}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-separates-orbits}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:838d9f4317773b10381625a2ee972ff32e6455e8eca50ab8d8cf671aab5d85bf", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn\nExample <REF_0001>\nwe show that being set-theoretically invariant is ``too weak'' a notion in\nthe category of algebraic spaces. A more geometric reformulation\nof what it means to be set-theoretically invariant or to separate orbits is in\nLemma <REF_0002>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:57ad4f618a74f1d851a1908c09f5c3d81264696c96da9f81315450efdca4dda0", "unit_id": "tag:048M:prose-0007"}
{"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "048M", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\phi : U \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$R$", "MATH_0003": "$k$", "MATH_0004": "$B$", "MATH_0005": "$U(k) \\to X(k)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-set-theoretically-invariant}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-set-theoretic-invariant}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ba3ac826bfa6bcad314062c53b952c0d04000b0e5ab249b521f651f6cecb642e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3a4f60e1dda87219cfe8930fda3327dc6e6b492537b192500890e0475df5b881", "source_text": "In the situation of Definition <REF_0001>.\nA morphism <MATH_0001> is set-theoretically <MATH_0002>-invariant if and\nonly if for any algebraically closed field <MATH_0003> over <MATH_0004> the map\n<MATH_0005> is constant on orbits.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7e77a4f74b5b0fdf6184e85c8f8c0e4384db3a46c640180966227b65dcdcba70", "unit_id": "tag:048W:statement"}
{"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "048M", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$B$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a212586edce9af4a67c2675c32e9f8a532f26daed8e051996bd10c234e1198d3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:af79d87265d85abec908b11c56edf13e7442901622e7cf97dc3800a9f74aeb52", "source_text": "This is true because the condition is supposed to hold for all algebraically\nclosed fields over <MATH_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:04100e25ebca23f5dd723ef4cc0698e9352ee4a61add7b2965bb7b662228cfc8", "unit_id": "tag:048W:proof"}
